Die 3 rolled 12, which is higher than any face on die 1 (max 10) or die 2 (max 10). So the contract settles at **exactly 12**, and I hold no risk on my position.

Informed traders value the contract at exactly 12, so they won't trade against a quote that straddles 12. Noise traders value it at 12 plus Normal noise with standard deviation 2.1. I therefore pick the half-spread s that maximises s × P(noise > s). That optimum is about s ≈ 0.75σ ≈ 1.6, which gives roughly 0.36 expected profit per side.

